            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "will be lower in relation to the lead screw than formerly. Likewise the rack may have to be lowered to prevent excessive play in the handwheel. Adjustments of this nature, though essential, do not pertain to the subject matter of this book and therefore will not be discussed further. However, the importance of the LeadScrew in the efficient operation of the machine justifies the space allotted to several tests concerning its alignment to the halfnut and the bed ways. These matters will now be discussed.",
